      "id": "synchronous-transfer",
      "text": "On an open pipe, a Write of three bytes can pair with a one-byte Read, which copies one byte, sends an acknowledgment, and returns (1, nil). The writer advances by one byte and waits for another Read to consume the remaining two before returning (3, nil). A zero-length Read can acknowledge zero and return (0, nil) while a nonempty Write remains pending. A zero-length Write still waits for a Read to acknowledge zero before succeeding.",
      "citation": {
